{
  "$comment": "Red-flag interceptor rules for the Chat Guide. These run BEFORE scoring and force a specific KB entry regardless of the match score. They exist because scoring alone cannot see urgency: 'mataas ang presyon niya at sumasakit ang dibdib niya' scores highest against m1-hypertension-definition (a textbook definition) and never reaches m3-very-high-with-symptoms, which is the entry that says to arrange transport now. Rules are evaluated in array order and the first match wins, so more specific rules (those with and_any_of) are listed first. Phrases are matched whole-token against the normalized question, so 'hilo' does NOT match inside 'nahihilo' — every variant a BHW might type is listed explicitly, which is also what makes this list reviewable by a nurse rather than by a programmer. Every entry_id must be a published (tier: cited) entry; scripts/lib/kb-content.mjs enforces that.",
